<title>GERMANY: Bayer - unit to sell food additives business.</title>
<headline>Bayer - unit to sell food additives business.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group Bayer AG said on Friday that its unit Haarmann &amp; Reimer GmbH intends to sell its food additives business.</p>
<p>Bayer said that the group would like to sell the business, posting annual turnover of $293 million, as a whole rather than splitting it up and would initiate contact with potentially interested parties soon.</p>
<p>The planned sale would include production sites in the U.S, the U.K. and Brazil.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
